  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Gulfam Ansari vs State Of Kerala on 27 November, 2025 2025:Ker:91606 Crl.M.C.No.4297 & 2890 of 2020 1 In The High Court Of Kerala At Ernakulam Present The Honourable Mr. Justice G.Girish Thursday, The 27Th Day Of November 2025 / 6Th Agrahayana, 1947 Crl.Mc No. 4297 Of 2020 Crime No.428/2020 Of Kothamangalam Police Station, Ernakulam Against The Order/Judgment Dated In Cc No.220 Of 2020 Of Judicial First Class Magistrate Court - Ii, Kothamangalam Petitioner/S: 1 Gulfam Ansari Aged 33 Years S/O. Mohammed Ummar Ansari, H/S. 177, Nagarnigam, Saharanpur, Jain Colony, Uttar Pradesh, Now Residing At Kottarathil Koyon'S Buildings, Companypady, Nellikuzhy, Ernakulam District 2 Asif Aged 33 Years S/O. Mohammed Sakeer, Farman Basthi, Gadgeri, Saharnpur, Jain Colony, Uttar Pradesh, Now Residing At Kottarathil Koyon'S Buildings, Companpady,Nellikuzhy, Ernakulam District. 3 Shiyas, Aged 34 Years S/O. Mohammed, Kottarathil House, Schoolpady, Eramalloor Village, Nellikuzhy, Ernakulam District. By Advs. Sri.Deepak Raj Smt.C.P.Roopa Gulfam Ansari vs State Of Kerala on 27 November, 2025",
    "facts": "",
    "arguments": "For charging a person with the commission of offence under Section 118(e) of the Kerala Police Act, 2011, there should be sufficient materials to show that such person knowingly did any act, which caused danger to the public,or failure in public safety. 8. Section 120 of the Kerala Police Act, deals with the penalty for causing nuisance and violation of public order. The offence under Section 120(o) of the Kerala Police Act will be attracted, if it is shown that a person, by way of any means of communication, caused nuisance of himself to any other person by repeated or undesirable or anonymous call, letter, writing, message, e-mail or through a messenger.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": "For charging a person with the commission of offence under Section 118(e) of the Kerala Police Act, 2011, there should be sufficient materials to show that such person knowingly did any act, which caused danger to the public,or failure in public safety. 8. Section 120 of the Kerala Police Act, deals with the penalty for causing nuisance and violation of public order. The offence under Section 120(o) of the Kerala Police Act will be attracted, if it is shown that a person, by way of any means of communication, caused nuisance of himself to any other person by repeated or undesirable or anonymous call, letter, writing, message, e-mail or through a messenger."
  },
